Bugfix: Plural forms work under a Content Security Policy without unsafe-eval

The web interface built the plural rule of every translation bundle with
new Function. Under a Content Security Policy without 'unsafe-eval' this threw
an EvalError for each bundle on every page, and plural translations failed.
The plural rules are now read by a small parser for the gettext syntax and give
the same results as before. A plural rule that cannot be read falls back to the
default rule with a warning instead of an error.
